    why: "Real-time means correct and on time. The ChipCamp roadmap uses the Apollo 11 landing computer, which kept critical tasks running during overload, as the classic illustration of why priority scheduling matters.",
    problem: "Superloops work until a slow task delays an urgent one; without analysis you cannot promise a deadline will be met.",
